  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In a February 2025 official statement, Feinberg said AI is an overused term and much of it is high-end data analytics, while stressing partnership between operators and technologists. In official statements in the same hearing record, he said that if confirmed he would prioritize leading-edge AI capabilities, expand operationalization of Project Maven, scale AI solutions, and use AI to advance department priorities such as the audit. He also said using AI involves a difficult balance between authorities and lethality, and that developing autonomous capabilities with mass drones and a central brain is urgent for national security. In an October 2026 memorandum as Deputy Secretary of War, he appointed the Secretary of the Air Force as executive agent for ACME, a suite of AI-aided classification tools.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s5",
    "s7",
